ster and fields the large  investment alone means there will be no  move isn't it you never know what will  get used or not but I can't see it  happening our Tod is commerce net force  to the US has also invested a lot in  modern warfare in recent years the Air  and Space Operations Center is located  at the air base it's one of the u.s.  military's data hubs it is now an open  secret that Ramstein and plays a central  role in US drone strikes  important information on targets our  relates to the US via Ramstein opponents  of the base are unhappy about  preparations for war being made in  Germany for them a u.s. withdrawal would  be a reason to celebrate  but most people in Ramstein disagree  Germans and Americans have grown  together over the decades as seen at the  german-american friendship fest among  the guests are form and active members  of the military who don't believe the  airbase will be relocated how a.m. sight  is a central point in Europe for the  whole American forces and not only a  Europe at Africa's Middle East  everything is centered around Ramstein  and that's why this place is gonna stay  here look carefully at the airbase more  than a thousand buildings many of them  underground I know the place for that  reason they can't move at all to Poland  the Trump administration's threats to  relocate are something people in  Ramstein cannot imagine will ever happen  the joint location is too important for  both Americans and Germans let's bring  in our political correspondent Simon  Young here Simon  we just heard for some analysts and  people in Ramstein saying that they  don't believe that that the US will be  pulling its troops out of Germany  anytime soon but what about the  political establishment here in Berlin  do policymakers here take Trump's threat  seriously well certainly Chancellor  Merkel has said that she's not unduly  concerned about this she believes that  American troops are here to stay  and politicians generally point out but  as we